WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.400
A customer places an order. Three services have to react — and soon, a fourth. A queue, a topic, or an event bus?

2
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.500
This is ArchIQ. Your architecture decision guide for AWS — and Solutions Architect coach.

3
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:27.400
It starts with the service — a decision page, not a definition. When to use it, when not to, the trade-offs, the exact exam wording, the traps. One service, this deep.

4
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:39.900
Then it puts the close calls side by side. SQS keeps a message fourteen days; SNS doesn't persist at all. That's the decision.

5
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.300
And it names the trap. One shared queue can't fan out — delete a message, and it's gone for everyone else.

6
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:54.200
So it doesn't hand you a letter. It makes you choose — then explains why each answer is right, wrong, or only sometimes right.

7
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:05.600
And it isn't a question bank — it's a system. A dozen ways to study all a hundred and eighteen services: comparisons, guides, flashcards, traps, a tutor.

8
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.800
Because nobody accepts "the docs said so." It doesn't teach you the answer — it teaches you to defend it.

9
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.400
Reason through the decision. Then pass the exam. ArchIQ — think like an architect.
